//? Title: Manacher byte-palindrome radii
//? Subtitle: Actual mirror reuse, safe tagged controls and the original abacaba radii
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Manacher reuses a mirrored radius inside the rightmost known palindrome and
tests only what remains uncertain. We retain the original abacaba radius array
and leftmost-longest policy, expose real mirror/expansion decisions, and replace
collision-prone character sentinels with distinct integer tags so every input
byte is supported safely.
)

\toc

> Tiny mirrored radius on aba

Insert a separator between original bytes and at both ends, then distinct
left/right guards. Odd and even byte palindromes become radii centered at
transformed symbols. At center i inside the known inclusive right frontier R
with stored center C, initialize radius to min(p[2*C−i],R−i). The cap prevents
mirror reuse from asserting anything beyond the known frontier. Then compare
actual symmetric symbols until a mismatch or explicit bound is reached, and
advance the stored frontier only if i+p[i] is strictly greater.

The tiny aba example has a real reused positive mirror radius near the end of
its scan. The table shows every actual center, while the diagram selects that
one real initialization and its final radius. The diagram is not a second
palindrome expansion or a fabricated prefix history.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/manacher_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/manacher.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::manacher_trace("aba");
    std::print("| actual center | prior frontier center | prior inclusive right | reuse | actual mirror or " "SIZE_MAX | mirror radius | actual cap | initial radius | final radius | actual new right " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &c : t.centers)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                   c.index, c.center_before, c.right_before, c.reused, c.mirror,
                   c.mirror_radius, c.bound, c.initial, c.final, c.right_after);
    auto it = std::find_if(t.centers.begin(), t.centers.end(), [](auto &c) {
        return c.reused && c.initial > 0;
    });
    auto &c = *it;
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("mirror", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual mirror{} radius{}\nknown frontier cap{}",
                       c.mirror, c.mirror_radius, c.bound)).node(
        "initial", {6, 0},
        std::format("Actual center{} initial{}\nselected capped reuse", c.index,
                    c.initial)).node("final", {12, 0},
                                     std::format("Actual final radius{}\nright frontier{}",
                                                 c.final, c.right_after)).edge(
        "mirror", "initial").edge("initial", "final");
    d.save_svg("build/manacher_tiny.svg");
}
```
