> Literal punctuation cannot masquerade as a sentinel

The former implementation inserted character controls ^,#,$ into an unrestricted
byte string and assumed they could match nothing in the input. A literal ^ could
match the left guard during expansion and lead to an out-of-bounds index;
literal separator bytes could also yield incorrect byte-length radii. The new
producer uses integer tags outside the byte domain and explicit safe index
bounds. It accepts every byte value, including embedded NULs and high bytes,
while preserving ordinary sentinel-free ASCII results.

For the original input bytes ^#^, the actual longest palindrome is all three
bytes. Its original byte0x5E is distinct from tagged left guard257, and byte0x23
is distinct from separator256. The diagram and table show those real producer
values. Matching is byte-sensitive: a palindromic UTF-8 byte sequence and a
palindromic Unicode codepoint/grapheme sequence are different problems.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/manacher_tags.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/manacher.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::manacher_trace("^#^");
    std::print("| actual transformed index | actual integer symbol | native role label | actual radius |\n| " "---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.symbols.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, t.symbols[i],
                   dm::algorithms::manacher_symbol_label(t.symbols[i]),
                   t.analysis.radii[i]);
    std::print("\nActual selected start {}; actual byte length {}; native run `{}`.\n",
               t.analysis.longest.start, t.analysis.longest.length,
               t.input.substr(t.analysis.longest.start,
                              t.analysis.longest.length));
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("guard", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual left guard tag{}\n{}", t.symbols[0],
                       dm::algorithms::manacher_symbol_label(t.symbols[0]))).node("byte", {6, 0}, std::format("Actual original byte{}\n{}", t.symbols[2], dm::algorithms::manacher_symbol_label(t.symbols[2]))).node("result", {12, 0}, std::format("Actual byte palindrome length{}\nno tag collision", t.analysis.longest.length)).edge("guard", "byte", "different tags").edge("byte", "result");
    d.save_svg("build/manacher_tags.svg");
}
