> Why comparisons remain linear

There are exactly2*n+1 nonsentinel centers. A reused mirror radius strictly
inside its frontier cap cannot grow: its next real comparison must fail by
reflected palindrome symmetry. A radius reaching the cap can grow only by
testing new positions beyond the prior right frontier. Every successful
expansion therefore consumes progress in a frontier that never retreats, while
each center contributes at most one failed terminating equality test. This
yields O(n) actual comparisons and O(n) storage.

The old header overstated this as every comparison advancing right. Failed
comparisons do not advance it, and neither does mere mirror reuse. The native
counts below separate actual successful expansions, total comparisons and actual
frontier updates. Prescribed repeated-byte inputs are independent count-only
studies, not prefix replay for reconstructing a trace.

Complete2*n+3 transform/radius geometry is checked before allocation. Complete
trace admission initially counts n original bytes plus twice the transform
length for actual symbols/final radii, then each real center/comparison record
before copying. Default cap is one million; zero disables only that optional
cap. Fields, capacities, result/runtime copies and physical bytes are excluded.
Unknown future comparisons are not fabricated; a trace is complete or throws.
Empty input has three transformed symbols and one real separator-center
mismatch, with zero longest length and start.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/manacher_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/manacher.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y, z;
    std::print("| prescribed repeated input bytes | actual centers | actual reused mirrors | actual " "successful expansions | actual comparisons including failures | actual frontier updates " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256}) {
        auto a = dm::algorithms::manacher_analyze(std::string(n, 'a'));
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, a.work.centers,
                   a.work.mirror_reuses, a.work.expansions, a.work.comparisons,
                   a.work.frontier_updates);
        x.push_back(n);
        y.push_back(a.work.comparisons);
        z.push_back(a.work.expansions);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "all comparisons", {37, 99, 235}, 2).line(
        x, z, "successful expansions", {22, 163, 74}, 2).title(
        "Actual Manacher work on repeated-byte controls").x_label(
        "prescribed original byte count").y_label("actual selected native operations").save_svg("build/manacher_work.svg");
}
```
