> Verification and references

Native tests enumerate511 binary words through length eight and1093
sentinel-byte words through length six, independently enumerate every raw
substring to recover each centered radius and leftmost optimum, and inspect
every actual mirror/comparison/frontier record. They retain the original exact
radius array, odd/even and leftmost ties, all256 byte values,500 arbitrary-byte
inputs, explicit caret/separator/NUL controls, complete quotas, native tag
labels, empty behavior and ownership. Existing4000 random-string brute-force
regression cases remain. The ten-report batch passes 95 CTest cases, 30 directly
instrumented ASan/UBSan cases, 121 compiled and executed public examples,
601/601 scoped documentation definitions and 11 representative hovers.
Independent integer, Fraction, graph, string and NumPy references verify 82,729
records, including the complete original seeded LSH study. Frozen comparisons
preserve ordinary legacy results; malformed-input, sentinel-collision, ownership
and explicit-budget corrections are documented above. Thirteen checkout headers
and thirteen installed headers compile independently, and an installed-header
native consumer links and runs. Each complete report program runs against the
checkout library; all four native figures are reviewed and HTML/Markdown exports
preserve computed results and image bytes. Batch receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-214-223/`.

G. Manacher(1975),
[A New Linear-Time On-Line Algorithm for Finding the Smallest Initial Palindrome of a String|https://doi.org/10.1145/321892.321896],
Journal of the ACM22(3),346–351. This report uses the modern full-radius mirror
formulation to find the longest contiguous byte palindrome, with explicit
tagged-control and finite-container contracts for this implementation.
